## Goal
Deploy TaskMaster (Angular static dashboard + NestJS API) to Azure with IaC and GitHub Actions on push to main. Provision required Azure resources automatically on first deployment, using only free tiers.

## Project Information
- Name: TaskMaster
- Monorepo: Nx with two apps and shared libs
  - Frontend: Angular 20 static build at `dist/apps/dashboard/browser`
  - Backend: NestJS 11 API listening on `PORT` (defaults 3001), global prefix `/api`
  - DB: SQLite file (local). For Azure Free, we avoid a server DB; API can still run with SQLite for demo, but ephemeral filesystem applies.
- Recommended hosting:
  - Frontend: Azure Static Web Apps (Free)
  - API: Azure App Service Linux Free (F1)

## Azure Resources Architecture
```mermaid
flowchart LR
  User((User)) --> SWA[Azure Static Web Apps (Free)]
  SWA -->|/api/* reverse proxy| API[Azure App Service (Linux F1) - NestJS]
```

Data flow:
- User accesses SWA; static files served from SWA. Requests to `/api/*` are routed to the API.
- API processes JWT auth/RBAC and uses TypeORM against local SQLite (demo) storage.

## Recommended Azure Resources
- Frontend (Static Web App)
  - Service: Static Web Apps Free
  - Build: `apps/dashboard` -> output `dist/apps/dashboard/browser`
  - routes.json: proxy `/api/*` to API URL
- Backend (Web App)
  - Service: Azure App Service (Linux, Node 20, Free F1)
  - App settings:
    - PORT=8080 (App Service uses 8080 by convention)
    - NODE_ENV=production
    - JWT_SECRET (set in GitHub Secrets and App Settings)
  - Startup command: `node dist/apps/api/main.js`
  - Deployment: GitHub Actions using OIDC
- Monitoring
  - (Optional) Application Insights (Basic). To keep fully free, omit for now.

Security configurations
- Use GitHub OIDC for Actions to deploy without storing secrets.
- Store JWT_SECRET in GitHub Secrets and sync to App Settings.

## Execution Steps
1) Generate IaC (Bicep) for:
   - Static Web App (Free)
   - Linux Web App (Free F1) + Node 20 runtime
   - Resource Group
2) Validate Bicep syntax.
3) Provision with `azd up` (or group deployments with what-if first).
4) Configure SWA routes to proxy `/api/*` to the API.
5) Set up GitHub Actions workflows to build and deploy both apps on push to `main`.
6) First run provisions resources if missing; subsequent runs deploy only.
